{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Adopt the Spring Cloud Stream annotation-based programming model (@EnableBinding, @Source, @Sink) as the target model for all modules ported from Spring XD (U6, U7, U8).",
    "U1: Register the hdfs sink in the Spring Cloud Data Flow module registry as a sink application with generated configuration metadata (configuration properties) so it can be referenced in stream definitions.",
    "U2: Implement Hadoop shell commands in the Spring Cloud Data Flow shell by integrating Hadoop FileSystem access (via Spring for Apache Hadoop / hadoop-fs) and exposing a focused command set (e.g., fs ls, cat, mkdir, rm, chmod, put, get) rather than a full HDFS CLI clone.",
    "U3: Run a time-boxed research spike comparing composed-job persistence options: (a) extending the existing Spring Batch job repository schema, (b) a dedicated composed-job definition repository keyed by name with a serialized graph, and (c) reusing XD module/deployment repositories; recommend (b) as the basis for U4.",
    "U4: Implement composed jobs using a simple composition DSL parsed into a directed graph, persisted through the repository chosen in U3, and executed by a coordinator that launches child job definitions in sequence/parallel with conditional transitions, plus shell and REST surfaces.",
    "U6: Implement XD-like property binding in Spring Cloud Stream via SpEL expression evaluation and header-to-property mapping so message payloads/properties can be bound to module inputs across binder implementations.",
    "U7/U8: Port jdbc (sink) and kafka (source) modules by adapting existing XD module code to the Spring Cloud Stream binder model, replacing XD-specific XML/container wiring with Spring Boot auto-configuration and externalized configuration properties.",
    "U5: Build a shell test harness that runs shell commands against an in-memory/mock admin server so command parsing, options handling, and output formatting are tested without deploying real streams.",
    "Use the existing multi-project Gradle builds of s-c-s and s-c-d, Java 8 baseline consistent with the current projects, JUnit 4 with Spring Test, and Mockito for isolation; use Hadoop mini-cluster for hdfs-related tests.",
    "Treat code review, documentation, and integration verification as explicit WBS activities rather than absorbing them into implementation tasks."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "A single developer performs all work; estimates are effort in work-hours, not elapsed duration.",
    "The developer is already familiar with the Spring XD, Spring Cloud Stream, and Spring Cloud Data Flow codebases, reducing ramp-up and porting effort.",
    "A Hadoop mini-cluster (test harness) is available for hdfs sink and hadoop shell command testing; no real Hadoop cluster setup effort is included beyond local test configuration.",
    "The linked Google document for U5 is inaccessible; standard shell-command isolation testing scope is assumed (parsing, validation, output formatting, error handling for existing commands).",
    "XD-2250 implies the jdbc module already exists in XD and requires adaptation to the s-c-s model, not a rewrite from scratch; same assumption applies to the kafka module.",
    "U3 is a spike producing a written recommendation and prototype; its output feeds U4, and U4's estimate assumes option (b) from the spike is chosen.",
    "Scope covers implementation, unit tests, and basic integration tests plus developer documentation; production hardening, performance tuning, CI pipeline changes, and release engineering beyond a basic release prep pass are excluded.",
    "No changes to binder implementations (e.g., kafka binder internals) are needed for U6/U8 beyond module-level adaptation.",
    "Estimates assume steady, uninterrupted work and typical defect-fix cycles discovered during the developer's own testing."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Project setup and development environment",
      "activity_description": "Clone and build the s-c-s and s-c-d multi-module projects, set up IDE/tooling, configure a local Hadoop mini-cluster test fixture, and verify baseline builds and existing test suites run green before changes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Register hdfs sink in module registry",
      "activity_description": "Add the hdfs sink application to the Spring Cloud Data Flow module registry as a sink: create/adjust module coordinates, generate and validate configuration metadata, wire registration defaults, and add unit tests verifying the module is resolvable in stream definitions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Hadoop commands in shell",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement Hadoop filesystem commands in the Spring Cloud Data Flow shell (fs ls, cat, mkdir, rm, chmod, put, get), including Hadoop FileSystem configuration via spring-data-hadoop, option parsing, output formatting, error handling, and unit/integration tests against the mini-cluster.",
      "most_likely_effort": 40
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Composed jobs repository options spike",
      "activity_description": "Time-boxed research spike evaluating repository options for composed job definitions (extend Spring Batch job repository, dedicated composed-job repository storing a serialized graph, or reuse of XD repositories); produce a written comparison, prototype the recommended option, and document the decision feeding U4.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4: Composed jobs orchestration",
      "activity_description": "Implement composed jobs end to end: composition DSL definition and parser, directed graph model with sequential/parallel/conditional transitions, persistence via the repository selected in U3, a coordinator/execution engine that launches and monitors child jobs, shell and REST surfaces for create/list/launch/destroy, and unit plus integration tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 120
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Isolated shell command test harness",
      "activity_description": "Create an abstract test harness that executes shell commands against an in-memory/mock admin layer (no real stream deployments), then migrate/add test coverage for existing shell commands covering parsing, validation, output formatting, and error paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 48
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U6: Expression-based message binding in s-c-s",
      "activity_description": "Implement XD-like binding of incoming messages to module inputs in Spring Cloud Stream: SpEL-based evaluation of message payload/properties, header-to-property mapping, binder-agnostic configuration, and unit/integration tests across at least one binder to validate behavior.",
      "most_likely_effort": 64
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U7: Port jdbc module (sink) from XD to s-c-s",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD jdbc module into the Spring Cloud Stream repository as a sink: adapt XD wiring to @EnableBinding(Sink.class) and Spring Boot auto-configuration, externalize configuration properties, update build/packaging, port and extend tests, and verify against an embedded database.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U8: Port kafka module (source) from XD to s-c-s",
      "activity_description": "Move the XD kafka module into the Spring Cloud Stream repository as a source: adapt to @EnableBinding(Source.class) and the kafka binder, externalize configuration properties, update build/packaging, port and extend tests, and verify against an embedded/local kafka broker.",
      "most_likely_effort": 32
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration and end-to-end verification",
      "activity_description": "Run cross-feature integration checks: hdfs sink resolvable in a stream definition and writing via mini-cluster, hadoop shell commands against the same fixture, composed job workflow execution end to end, and kafka-source to jdbc-sink pipeline smoke test; fix defects found.",
      "most_likely_effort": 24
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and samples",
      "activity_description": "Write developer- and user-facing documentation: reference docs for hdfs sink registration, hadoop shell commands, composed job DSL and orchestration usage, expression-based binding configuration, and migration notes for the ported jdbc and kafka modules, plus minimal samples.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Code review, refactoring, and release preparation",
      "activity_description": "Self-review and clean up all changes (style, javadoc, license headers, checkstyle compliance), address review feedback from maintainers, rebase/squash branches, update changelogs, and prepare pull requests for each story.",
      "most_likely_effort": 16
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 448
  }
}

